---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import markPortrait from '../../images/MarkPro.webp';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <section class="hero-home">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">FDA research systems / applied AI / AWS architecture</p>
      <h1><em>Stop spending money to make bad processes faster. Eliminate them. It’s free.</em></h1>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-aside" data-reveal>
      <p>I lead modernization work for FDA’s Research Tracking System (RTS). I’m leading its first LLM integration and planning its replatform to AWS, connecting technical decisions to the mission, people, and investment behind them.</p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button primary" href="/work/#rts-ai">See the RTS work <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
        <a class="button" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/markgingrass/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Hire me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="proof-rail" aria-label="Career at a glance">
    <div class="proof-grid">
      <div class="proof-item"><strong>37</strong><span>Weapon systems</span></div>
      <div class="proof-item"><strong>12,000</strong><span>Engines</span></div>
      <div class="proof-item"><strong>$6.3B+</strong><span>Annual budget authority</span></div>
      <div class="proof-item"><strong>15M+</strong><span>Records integrated in CIRDS</span></div>
      <div class="proof-item"><strong>400+</strong><span>Regulatory scientists served</span></div>
      <div class="proof-item"><strong>GS-14</strong><span>Program leadership / COR III · 20+ years in federal technology</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="proof-note">The weapon systems, engines, and budget figures are from my previous role as a logistics supply chain manager for 448 SCMW.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell case-grid">
      <div class="case-intro" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Research Tracking System / applied AI</p>
        <h3>Bring an LLM into RTS. Keep scientists in control.</h3>
        <p>I’m leading the first AI integration into FDA’s Research Tracking System. The LLM compares project abstracts with the governing coding manual, returns supporting evidence, and flags disagreements. FDA reviewers make the final call.</p>
        <p>In parallel, I’m leading planning to replatform RTS to AWS. That work sets the architecture and migration direction for eventual modernization while the current research mission continues.</p>
        <a class="button link" href="/work/#rts-ai">See the RTS work <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="case-steps" data-reveal>
        <div class="case-step"><span>01</span><div><h4>Constrain the task</h4><p>Analyze against an authoritative manual—not an open-ended prompt.</p></div></div>
        <div class="case-step"><span>02</span><div><h4>Show the evidence</h4><p>Return supporting snippets and discrepancy flags with each recommendation.</p></div></div>
        <div class="case-step"><span>03</span><div><h4>Preserve accountability</h4><p>Use AI to narrow the discussion; keep decision authority with reviewers.</p></div></div>
        <div class="case-step"><span>04</span><div><h4>Fit the environment</h4><p>Operate within the agency boundary and the existing review process.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <SectionHeading
        label="Operating range"
        title="Get rid of the buzzwords. I’m solving a real problem. Before spending money on technology, I look at what we can simplify, change, or stop doing altogether."
        body="I take mission priorities and connect them to the investment, acquisition, architecture, and product decisions needed to move forward. I know where those pieces overlap, where they get stuck, and who to bring together to get things done."
      />
      <div class="role-grid">
        <article class="role-card" data-reveal>
          <h3>Strategic direction</h3>
          <p>I set the direction, prioritize through both an enterprise and product owner lens, get the right people involved, and work with the team all the way through implementation.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="role-card" data-reveal>
          <h3>Technical judgment</h3>
          <p>I look past the technical solution itself, challenge the assumptions behind it, and connect the decisions back to the mission and business need.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="role-card" data-reveal>
          <h3>Delivery accountability</h3>
          <p>I establish clear ownership, address problems early, and keep teams and vendors focused on building something that actually works for the people using it.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="role-card" data-reveal>
          <h3>Vendor leadership</h3>
          <p>I’ve led complex vendor environments for years, from onboarding new teams to coordinating multiple vendors, subcontractors, and projects running at the same time.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section paper">
    <div class="shell">
      <SectionHeading
        label="Architecture in practice / TutorialRepo"
        title="A working system is one proof point."
        body="I direct TutorialRepo across AWS delivery, AI, a publishing pipeline, and a native iOS client. The platform supports more courses on one foundation, and I carry the architecture decisions through release and operation."
      />
      <a class="button dark-button" href="/work/#tutorialrepo">See the architecture decisions <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="identity-panel">
    <div class="portrait-wrap">
      <Image src={markPortrait} alt="Mark Gingrass in his home office" widths={[640, 960, 1280]} sizes="(max-width: 980px) 100vw, 42vw" loading="eager" />
    </div>
    <div class="identity-copy">
      <div>
        <p class="micro-label">The through-line</p>
        <blockquote>Solve the real problem.</blockquote>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Air Force veteran. Electrical engineering and computer science background. MBA. GS-14 program manager and COR III. I’ve spent more than 20 years in federal technology. I know how programs get stuck, how vendors drift, and how good technical decisions get lost. I expect technology investments to produce something useful and justify what they cost. I also know how to get the work moving again.</p>
        <a class="button" href="/profile/">More about how I operate <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section compact">
    <div class="shell">
      <SectionHeading index="02" label="Field notes" title="Writing about systems, incentives, and the decisions between them." />
      <div class="writing-grid">
        <a class="writing-card" href="https://newsletter.markgingrass.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" data-reveal>
          <span class="micro-label">Federal IT</span><h3>The certificate warning nobody reads</h3><p>Read on Substack ↗</p>
        </a>
        <a class="writing-card" href="https://newsletter.markgingrass.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" data-reveal>
          <span class="micro-label">Applied AI</span><h3>The AI solution trap</h3><p>Read on Substack ↗</p>
        </a>
        <a class="writing-card" href="https://newsletter.markgingrass.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" data-reveal>
          <span class="micro-label">All dispatches</span><h3>Notes from the intersection of public mission and modern technology.</h3><p>Browse the newsletter ↗</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
